{
  "slug": "shazam",
  "name": "Shazam",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A skill-based workflow plugin for planning, architecture,    and bug triage. 18 skills covering the full development cycle: write PRDs, break them into plans and issues, improve    codebase architecture, triage bugs, and more. Just shout out SHAZAM! for a navigation guide that suggests what to do    next based on your current context. Soft suggestions, no   forced workflows — you stay in control.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **18 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (18): `design-an-interface` (Generate multiple radically different interface designs for a module using parallel sub-agents), `edit-article` (Edit and improve articles by restructuring sections, improving clarity, and tightening prose), `git-guardrails-claude-code` (Set up Claude Code hooks to block dangerous git commands (push, reset --hard, clean, branch -D, etc.) before…), `github-triage` (Triage GitHub issues through a label-based state machine with interactive grilling sessions), `grill-me` (Interview the user relentlessly about a plan or design until reaching shared understanding, resolving each branch of the…), `improve-codebase-architecture` (Explore a codebase to find opportunities for architectural improvement, focusing on making the codebase more testable by deepening…), `migrate-to-shoehorn` (Migrate test files from `as` type assertions to @total-typescript/shoehorn), `obsidian-vault` (Search, create, and manage notes in the Obsidian vault with wikilinks and index notes), and 10 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install shazam@claude-community` from `qhuang20/shazam`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
